{"metadata":{"title":"PassthroughSubject","symbolKind":"class","fragments":[{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"PassthroughSubject","kind":"identifier"}],"remoteSource":{"fileName":"PassthroughSubject.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Afluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Afluent\/PassthroughSubject.swift#L41"},"externalID":"s:7Afluent18PassthroughSubjectC","roleHeading":"Class","role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"Afluent"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"PassthroughSubject","kind":"identifier"}]},"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent"]]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/PassthroughSubject","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/afluent\/passthroughsubject"]}],"kind":"symbol","relationshipsSections":[{"type":"conformsTo","title":"Conforms To","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Afluent\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/Afluent\/s16SendableMetatypeP","doc:\/\/Afluent\/Sci"],"kind":"relationships"}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"text":"final","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"class","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"kind":"identifier","text":"PassthroughSubject"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Element"},{"kind":"text","text":"> "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Element"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:s8SendableP","text":"Sendable"}],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Subscribing","level":2,"anchor":"Subscribing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A consumer subscribes when its iterator is created, which is when a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"for try await"},{"type":"text","text":" loop over the subject"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(or over an operator chain built on it) begins. From then on, every value sent is buffered for that consumer"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"until it is consumed, so a consumer that is slower than the sender still sees every value, in order."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Values sent while there are no subscribers are discarded; they are never replayed to a later consumer.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"aside","style":"important","name":"Important","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Starting a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Task"},{"text":" that iterates the subject does not mean it has subscribed yet. If values must","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"not be missed, wait until the consumer has subscribed before sending, for example with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"handleEvents(receiveMakeIterator:)"},{"text":".","type":"text"}]}]},{"type":"heading","text":"Example","level":2,"anchor":"Example"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let subject = PassthroughSubject<Int>()","let subscribed = SingleValueSubject<Void>()","","subject.send(0) \/\/ No subscribers yet, so this value is discarded.","","Task {","    for try await value in subject.handleEvents(receiveMakeIterator: { try? subscribed.send() }) {","        print(\"Received value: \\(value)\") \/\/ prints 1, then 2","    }","}","","try await subscribed.execute()","subject.send(1)","subject.send(2)","subject.send(completion: .finished)"]}],"kind":"content"}],"topicSections":[{"title":"Structures","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/PassthroughSubject\/Iterator"],"anchor":"Structures"},{"title":"Initializers","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/PassthroughSubject\/init()"],"anchor":"Initializers"},{"title":"Instance Methods","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/PassthroughSubject\/makeAsyncIterator()","doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/PassthroughSubject\/send()","doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/PassthroughSubject\/send(_:)","doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/PassthroughSubject\/send(completion:)"],"anchor":"Instance-Methods"},{"title":"Enumerations","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/PassthroughSubject\/Completion"],"anchor":"Enumerations"},{"title":"Default Implementations","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/PassthroughSubject\/AsyncSequence-Implementations","doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/PassthroughSubject\/AsyncSequence-Implementations"],"anchor":"Default-Implementations"}],"abstract":[{"text":"A subject that broadcasts values to multiple consumers without storing a current value.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Unlike ","type":"text"},{"code":"CurrentValueSubject","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"PassthroughSubject","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" does not retain the most recent value.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"This is an ","type":"text"},{"code":"AsyncSequence","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" that allows multiple tasks to asynchronously consume values and mimics Combine’s PassthroughSubject.","type":"text"}],"references":{"doc://Afluent/Sci":{"type":"unresolvable","identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/Sci","title":"_Concurrency.AsyncSequence"},"doc://Afluent/documentation/Afluent/PassthroughSubject/send(_:)":{"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"send","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"Element","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}],"type":"topic","title":"send(_:)","url":"\/documentation\/afluent\/passthroughsubject\/send(_:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Sends a n